From 088eb6bfd9e76d3b9fd838f672535a9a3d2c4ce4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JUI YU LIN <hlpmrlinyu@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 08:12:53 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] avcodec/ffv1dec: do not clamp the Golomb-Rice k to bits

put_vlc_symbol() in ffv1enc.c derives the Rice parameter k as

    i = state->count;
    k = 0;
    while (i < state->error_sum) { k++; i += i; }

and writes the symbol with that k. get_vlc_symbol() derives k with the same
loop but then clamps it to bits, so whenever k > bits the two sides use
different Rice parameters, the read consumes the wrong number of bits and the
remainder of the slice desyncs. Neither RFC 9043 nor the FFV1 v4 draft has
that clamp; both specify the bare loop.

The clamp used to be unreachable. For integer formats bits is 8..16, and since
fold() bounds the coded residual to [-(1 << (bits-1)), (1 << (bits-1)) - 1],
error_sum/count stays under 1 << bits, so k stays <= bits. FFV1 v4 remapping
breaks that: ff_ffv1_compute_bits_per_plane() takes the symbol width from the
remap table size, bits[p] = av_ceil_log2(remap_count[p]), which is 1 for any
slice plane holding only two distinct values. The initial VlcState
(error_sum = 4, count = 1) already walks the loop to k == 2, so such a plane
desyncs on its very first coded symbol.

The effect is a silently non-lossless round trip for every float pixel format
at default settings, since coder defaults to rice and float forces
remap_mode 2. gbrpf32le, gbrpf16le, grayf16le and yaf16le are all affected;
integer formats are not.

Keep a bound so damaged input cannot produce a negative shift inside
get_ur_golomb(), but use the encoder's own invariant (av_assert2(k <= 16) in
put_vlc_symbol) rather than bits.

Existing streams are not lost. With bits == 1 the unsigned Golomb value is 0
or 1, so e = i >> k is 0, far below limit == 12, and the escape branch - the
only one the decoder reads back at only esc_len == bits bits wide - is never
taken. Streams written by unpatched encoders therefore decode byte exactly
again with this change.

Signed-off-by: JUI YU LIN <hlpmrlinyu@gmail.com>
---
 libavcodec/ffv1dec.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libavcodec/ffv1dec.c b/libavcodec/ffv1dec.c
index 8de15d2..f2c0f9f 100644
--- a/libavcodec/ffv1dec.c
+++ b/libavcodec/ffv1dec.c
@@ -56,10 +56,10 @@ static inline int get_vlc_symbol(GetBitContext *gb, VlcState *const state,
         k++;
         i += i;
     }
-    if (k > bits) {
+    if (k > 16) {
         ff_dlog(NULL, "k-overflow bias:%d error:%d drift:%d count:%d k:%d",
                 state->bias, state->error_sum, state->drift, state->count, k);
-        k = bits;
+        k = 16;
     }
 
     v = get_sr_golomb(gb, k, 12, bits);
